<h1>Silvana Tabares</h1>
<p>23rd Ward alderman, on the Chicago ballot February 23, 2027. Incumbent.</p>
<h2>Running on</h2>
<p>Is seeking reelection and in September 2026 contributed $100,000 of her own money to her campaign, lifting contribution limits in the race. She says she is ready to keep providing essential services and bringing economic growth and new opportunities to the city, and points to her record on immigrant protections, constituent services from two ward offices, school improvements and public safety.</p>
<h2>Background</h2>
<p>23rd Ward alderwoman since 2018 (appointed, then elected in 2019); state representative for the 21st District from 2013 to 2018.</p>
